    "adapt": "The vanilla fuel-station shop (FuelStation_E_01_building, 10.9 x 5.5 m) is already furnished: a shop counter with its register prop at the -x end (local x -4.7, z -0.65, register at y 1.139), the street door on the +x wall at about z 0.35. The kit adds what the systems read: the attended till (meshless `LF_FuelTill_Attended`, on the register's own spot, so the robbery hold and the fuel_clerk dialogue find it), the fuel clerk behind the counter and the resident anchors (`counter` beside the clerk for the night-shift attendant, `door` on the forecourt by the street door). The slot's marker is the FuelTill place. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch. The two forecourt pumps (`pump-a`, `pump-b`) are LF_FuelPump (the vanilla tank pistol with the fuel station component, station id saint-philippe): each stands on the exact spot of a vanilla pump under the canopy, 3.5 m off the building front, so the vanilla pump under it is covered and its free refuel is switched off by the pump overlap check."
  },
